    "message": "test(upgrade): cover an IX_HOME containing a space\n\nThe one question from the #391/#392 review that the merged fixes did not\nanswer. #349's reporter is on `[local-path] 10` and their confirmed workaround\nwas pointing TEMP at a space-free path — and #392 moved the upgrade scratch from\n`[local-path] an 8.3 alias which never contains a\nspace, to `[local-path] 10\\.ix\\...`, which does. If that failure is space-driven\nrather than short-path-driven, the move put a space onto the upgrade path where\nthere previously was none.\n\nThis cannot settle the mechanism: it runs on whatever platform CI is on, and the\nsuspected fault is a Windows path provider. What it does is prove our own code\ncarries no space-free assumption, so when the reporter tries again the remaining\nsuspects are outside this repo. Nothing else in the suite passed a path with a\nspace.\n\nFour cases: preparing a download directory inside a spaced IX_HOME, creating one\nthat a manual install never made, sweeping orphans out of it, and restoring an\ninterrupted install into it.\n\nFound while writing them: the first version used `.cli-download-1-abc` and\nfailed, because pid 1 is init and always alive — the sweep correctly skipped it\nas an in-flight download owned by another process. That is `isLiveScratch`\nworking exactly as intended, and the test now uses a pid that is not running.\n\n759 green, tsc clean, lint unchanged (0 errors).",
